esword4linux (0.5.2-2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Declare the runtime system libraries as Build-Depends. Launchpad's clean
    Noble chroot failed in override_dh_auto_test because ldd could not resolve
    libglib-2.0.so.0, libgthread-2.0.so.0 and the other X11, Wayland and GL
    libraries used by the private Qt runtime. No code or runtime change.

 -- Felipe <felotrrs@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000

esword4linux (0.5.2-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Split the parallel comparison view into two stacked bands (the *Dividir*
    button, enabled from four versions on) whose vertical scrolls follow each
    other by verse. Both bands keep the same column count so the grid stays
    aligned and a new translation fills the free column.
  * Give the table-header band its own palette colour, always darker than the
    zebra rows, so it cannot be confused with the table body.
  * Never let the widget tests overwrite the user's real settings.json
    (conftest redirects the settings path), and read the packaged version from
    the runtime manifest instead of a hardcoded string.

 -- Felipe <felotrrs@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000

esword4linux (0.5.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Add the multi-version parallel Bible view: the *Vista paralela* shows the
    same chapter of several installed translations aligned by verse, with a
    native header coupled to the table columns and explicit missing
    book/chapter/verse states.
  * Fix the window behaviour: the resources panel no longer leaves an empty
    band when the app reopens with it collapsed, the Bible toolbar scrolls
    horizontally instead of dictating the window minimum, and the comparison
    strip no longer makes the window grow on every panel toggle.

 -- Felipe <felotrrs@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000

esword4linux (0.5.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial native Debian package for Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and Linux Mint 22.x.
  * Bundle PySide6-Essentials 6.12.0, shiboken6 6.12.0 and pure-Python
    PyYAML 6.0.3 in a private runtime under /opt/esword4linux.
  * Retain the X11 (xcb) and Wayland client Qt platform plugins together with
    the image-format plugins used by e-Sword modules.
  * Install the desktop entry, hicolor icons, man page and license texts.
  * Keep settings and indexes in the XDG user directories; never modify the
    user's e-Sword modules folder.

 -- Felipe <felotrrs@gmail.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000
